 "result_text": "`git machete github checkout-pr` now says \"PR #N is closed in repository `org/repo`\" when the PR exists but is closed. It keeps the \"is not found\" message when the PR doesn't exist. I haven't run it or the tests.\n\nThe open-PR list doesn't contain closed PRs. So when the number isn't in that list, the code now asks GitHub for that PR directly (`GET /repos/{org}/{repo}/pulls/{number}`) and checks whether its state is `closed`. The new helper is `is_pull_request_closed` in `git_machete/github.py`, called from `checkout_github_prs` in `git_machete/client.py`.\n\nThe helper treats any `MacheteException` from that lookup as \"not closed\", so the \"not found\" message is shown in those cases. The same exception also covers the 401, 403 and 404 responses, so a token or permission problem on the lookup would also end up as \"not found\" instead of showing the auth error.",
